1
00:00:04,105 --> 00:00:06,785
-<i>Just act natural at school, okay?</i>
-Putter!

2
00:00:07,305 --> 00:00:08,265
<i>That damage is insane.</i>

3
00:00:08,345 --> 00:00:09,745
<i>How am I supposed to handle it?</i>

4
00:00:09,825 --> 00:00:11,625
-Am I cute?
-Yeah.

5
00:00:11,705 --> 00:00:14,265
<i>What's with you? You're just too cute.</i>

6
00:00:15,705 --> 00:00:17,785
<i>You and Putter…</i>
<i>you're really not together, right?</i>

7
00:00:17,865 --> 00:00:19,265
<i>Are you doubting me?</i>

8
00:00:20,185 --> 00:00:21,345
<i>Then why did you lie to me?</i>

9
00:00:21,425 --> 00:00:23,025
<i>About going to Song Wat with Putter.</i>

10
00:00:23,105 --> 00:00:24,985
<i>If you don't want me</i>
<i>as your friend anymore,</i>

11
00:00:25,065 --> 00:00:26,865
then just say it, damn it!

12
00:00:26,945 --> 00:00:28,905
<i>Holy shit, Lee! Have you seen this?</i>

13
00:00:28,985 --> 00:00:30,745
<i>The Brain Drain gang found</i>
<i>Putter's alt account,</i>

14
00:00:30,825 --> 00:00:33,185
<i>and it looks like he likes Indy too.</i>

15
00:00:35,745 --> 00:00:37,225
-I've got your delivery.
-How much is it?

16
00:00:37,305 --> 00:00:38,465
That'll be 80 baht.

17
00:00:38,545 --> 00:00:39,585
-The transfer's complete.
-Got it.

18
00:00:39,665 --> 00:00:41,345
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you.

19
00:00:41,425 --> 00:00:43,065
-Enjoy your meal.
-Thank you.

20
00:00:54,465 --> 00:00:56,225
Hey, Ter.

21
00:00:56,305 --> 00:00:58,065
-Hey, Ter.
-Ter.

22
00:00:59,305 --> 00:01:01,865
-Ter.
-Putter.

23
00:01:01,945 --> 00:01:03,025
You're so sneaky.

24
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,704
You didn't tell us at all.

25
00:01:04,785 --> 00:01:06,065
Yeah.

26
00:01:06,585 --> 00:01:09,825
I knew it. I was wondering why he asked me
what perfume you wore that day.

27
00:01:11,305 --> 00:01:12,585
What's with you guys?

28
00:01:14,305 --> 00:01:15,505
You like Indy, don't you?

29
00:01:18,705 --> 00:01:20,545
Just admit it already.

30
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:22,665
-Gotcha!
-Busted!

31
00:01:22,745 --> 00:01:24,145
Come on, tell me.

32
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:25,385
Where did you hear that?

33
00:01:26,465 --> 00:01:27,785
From your alt account.

34
00:01:28,705 --> 00:01:29,585
Here.

35
00:01:30,785 --> 00:01:31,905
If you like him, just ask him out.

36
00:01:31,985 --> 00:01:32,985
What are you waiting for?

37
00:01:33,065 --> 00:01:34,425
-Don't be scared.
-Mr. President.

38
00:01:35,385 --> 00:01:36,625
I can, right?

39
00:01:36,705 --> 00:01:38,145
-Hey.
-Give me the go-ahead.

40
00:01:38,225 --> 00:01:40,465
I knew it. When you said you had a crush,

41
00:01:40,545 --> 00:01:42,105
you meant Indy, didn't you?

42
00:01:42,705 --> 00:01:43,545
Right?

43
00:01:45,905 --> 00:01:46,865
Of course.

44
00:01:46,945 --> 00:01:48,945
Why didn't you tell us?

45
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:39,865
Lee, just hear me out first. Lee!

46
00:02:39,945 --> 00:02:42,185
I'm listening. Go ahead and explain.

47
00:02:42,265 --> 00:02:43,545
It's true, isn't it?

48
00:02:45,305 --> 00:02:46,345
It used to be.

49
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:51,065
<i>I like Indie music too.</i>

50
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:53,345
How Indie are we talking?

51
00:02:53,945 --> 00:02:55,025
I listen to all kinds.

52
00:02:55,105 --> 00:02:56,865
Could you guys keep it down a little?

53
00:02:56,945 --> 00:02:59,625
<i>Long story short, we're in the same year.</i>

54
00:02:59,705 --> 00:03:02,385
I'm going to find out
who you have a crush on.

55
00:03:05,905 --> 00:03:07,265
But I don't like him anymore.

56
00:03:07,785 --> 00:03:10,705
I mean… You got over him that fast?

57
00:03:12,945 --> 00:03:14,025
Or…

58
00:03:14,105 --> 00:03:15,665
Are you using me as Indy's replacement?

59
00:03:15,745 --> 00:03:17,945
No. I really do like you.

60
00:03:21,225 --> 00:03:23,985
Lee. Lee.

61
00:03:24,945 --> 00:03:26,185
Just hear me out first.

62
00:03:28,385 --> 00:03:29,745
I think we should break up.

63
00:03:29,825 --> 00:03:33,025
I can't date someone who used to
have a crush on my best friend.

64
00:05:25,745 --> 00:05:27,225
Come on, let's take some pictures.

65
00:05:27,305 --> 00:05:28,945
No way. I'm not taking any.

66
00:05:29,025 --> 00:05:30,265
Come on.

67
00:05:56,145 --> 00:05:57,225
Look! This plushie is so cute.

68
00:05:58,505 --> 00:05:59,425
It's for you.

69
00:05:59,505 --> 00:06:02,025
This one's for you. Now we're even.

70
00:06:15,825 --> 00:06:17,145
Here. I got this for you.

71
00:06:28,025 --> 00:06:28,865
Shit.

72
00:06:28,945 --> 00:06:30,385
Proud.

73
00:06:32,545 --> 00:06:33,505
Indy.

74
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:38,945
PUTTER DEFINITELY LIKES INDY

75
00:06:39,025 --> 00:06:41,265
<i>Putter definitely likes Indy.</i>

76
00:06:41,345 --> 00:06:43,825
<i>So it's not Lee and Putter after all?</i>

77
00:06:43,905 --> 00:06:45,985
Wait, is this for real
or are they just stirring things up?

78
00:06:46,065 --> 00:06:49,505
The Brain Drain gang says
this really is Putter's account.

79
00:06:59,345 --> 00:07:00,305
Leo.

80
00:07:00,945 --> 00:07:03,585
Didn't you come to school
with Lee and Ter?

81
00:07:05,305 --> 00:07:06,425
Uh…

82
00:07:06,505 --> 00:07:08,825
Lee… I don't know what got him so upset.

83
00:07:08,905 --> 00:07:10,265
So Ter went after him.

84
00:07:10,345 --> 00:07:12,745
Hey, but we have practice today.

85
00:07:13,905 --> 00:07:15,145
I think…

86
00:07:17,105 --> 00:07:18,425
Let's just leave it for now.

87
00:07:19,025 --> 00:07:19,945
Trust me.

88
00:07:21,305 --> 00:07:24,625
I agree. I think we should
cancel practice today, Indy.

89
00:07:25,225 --> 00:07:28,265
Yeah… I'll go cancel
the room booking first.

90
00:08:10,665 --> 00:08:12,305
You should take a break.

91
00:08:14,665 --> 00:08:16,665
The more you force it,
the worse it'll get.

92
00:08:23,865 --> 00:08:24,825
Are you stressed?

93
00:08:26,625 --> 00:08:27,745
How could you tell?

94
00:08:32,705 --> 00:08:34,305
Your linework gave it away.

95
00:08:35,105 --> 00:08:36,105
It's shaky.

96
00:08:36,784 --> 00:08:38,664
You're usually much steadier than this.

97
00:08:47,145 --> 00:08:48,625
I'm fine.

98
00:08:48,705 --> 00:08:49,905
I'm just a little tired.

99
00:08:49,985 --> 00:08:52,105
I'll get some rest. I'll feel better soon.

100
00:08:53,065 --> 00:08:55,105
Go on, head home and get some rest.

101
00:08:55,185 --> 00:08:57,185
I'll save your attendance
credit this time.

102
00:09:00,425 --> 00:09:03,425
Hey, is LeeIth still taking the class?

103
00:09:03,505 --> 00:09:05,145
He already paid for the full course,

104
00:09:05,225 --> 00:09:06,585
but he hasn't shown up at all.

105
00:09:07,425 --> 00:09:08,505
I think…

106
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:12,665
he… probably changed his mind.

107
00:10:47,905 --> 00:10:48,865
I'm back!

108
00:10:49,385 --> 00:10:50,705
<i>Hey. Putter's here!</i>

109
00:10:52,265 --> 00:10:54,265
<i>The team we're scrimming against</i>
<i>are pretty good.</i>

110
00:10:54,345 --> 00:10:56,825
<i>We're all here now, right?</i>

111
00:10:56,905 --> 00:10:59,425
<i>Let's take it easy today, okay?</i>

112
00:11:07,505 --> 00:11:09,185
THIS IS NO ONE ELSE'S BUSINESS

113
00:11:09,265 --> 00:11:11,425
<i>This is no one else's business.</i>

114
00:11:16,985 --> 00:11:18,425
DEACTIVATE YOUR ACCOUNT

115
00:11:18,505 --> 00:11:19,385
DEACTIVATE

116
00:11:19,465 --> 00:11:20,545
<i>Are you guys ready?</i>

117
00:11:21,785 --> 00:11:24,105
Come on, everyone. Let's do this!

118
00:11:31,905 --> 00:11:35,585
INDY

119
00:11:47,705 --> 00:11:50,305
Indy, you've called a hundred times.
Stop calling.

120
00:11:54,025 --> 00:11:55,825
Both Ter and Lee…

121
00:11:55,905 --> 00:11:58,025
Damn, they've both disappeared.

122
00:11:58,105 --> 00:11:59,265
What the hell's going on with them?

123
00:11:59,345 --> 00:12:01,425
Maybe they're sick.

124
00:12:01,505 --> 00:12:06,145
Hey, I think…
it might be about Putter's alt account.

125
00:12:08,505 --> 00:12:09,505
What do you mean?

126
00:12:10,785 --> 00:12:13,905
Well…

127
00:12:17,305 --> 00:12:19,625
Well…

128
00:12:28,105 --> 00:12:29,225
Leo.

129
00:12:31,505 --> 00:12:33,425
Do you have something to say?

130
00:12:33,505 --> 00:12:35,065
Well…

131
00:12:35,825 --> 00:12:38,065
You know where they went, don't you?

132
00:12:51,665 --> 00:12:53,345
Well…

133
00:12:53,985 --> 00:12:59,225
I'm not really sure, but I think…

134
00:12:59,985 --> 00:13:01,145
Lee.

135
00:13:01,225 --> 00:13:03,505
<i>That day, Neo told me to go after them.</i>

136
00:13:03,585 --> 00:13:05,465
-<i>They were worried they'd start fighting.</i>
-Lee.

137
00:13:05,545 --> 00:13:06,945
Will you just hear me out?

138
00:13:07,025 --> 00:13:09,185
Let's break up.

139
00:13:09,265 --> 00:13:11,465
I can't date someone
who's in love with my best friend.

140
00:13:18,745 --> 00:13:19,905
Shit.

141
00:13:21,025 --> 00:13:22,465
When did they even start dating?

142
00:13:25,025 --> 00:13:26,385
Seriously, when did they get together?

143
00:13:26,465 --> 00:13:28,025
And they've already broken up?

144
00:13:29,065 --> 00:13:31,065
At first, I didn't believe it either.

145
00:13:31,145 --> 00:13:32,705
But after Leo told me,

146
00:13:32,785 --> 00:13:36,305
and with the way LeeIth
was acting all secretive,

147
00:13:36,385 --> 00:13:37,705
it all started to make sense.

148
00:13:37,785 --> 00:13:40,425
And… you weren't going to tell me?

149
00:13:40,505 --> 00:13:41,345
You traitorous twins.

150
00:13:42,145 --> 00:13:43,185
Uh…

151
00:13:43,705 --> 00:13:45,265
We had to respect our friends' privacy.

152
00:13:46,345 --> 00:13:48,265
I'm the only one who didn't know.

153
00:13:49,825 --> 00:13:52,265
He made the rules,
then broke them himself.

154
00:13:52,345 --> 00:13:53,825
That's my badass president.

155
00:13:54,425 --> 00:13:56,985
Maybe that's why he doesn't
want to face us.

156
00:13:58,265 --> 00:14:00,265
Why are you all gossiping here?

157
00:14:00,345 --> 00:14:01,665
Don't you have a club room?

158
00:14:01,745 --> 00:14:03,585
The club room isn't safe anymore.

159
00:14:03,665 --> 00:14:05,785
We can't let outsiders
find out about this.

160
00:14:07,985 --> 00:14:09,585
Then why am I allowed to know?

161
00:14:09,665 --> 00:14:11,385
You're not an outsider.

162
00:14:11,465 --> 00:14:12,985
I already consider you a friend.

163
00:14:13,065 --> 00:14:15,545
Besides, I know you already knew.

164
00:14:15,625 --> 00:14:18,385
I know nothing. I'm going back to sleep.

165
00:14:18,465 --> 00:14:20,505
Then let's get the plan started.

166
00:14:20,585 --> 00:14:22,265
Everyone, take out your phones.

167
00:14:25,625 --> 00:14:26,905
<i>I miss you guys.</i>

168
00:14:26,985 --> 00:14:27,985
I MISS YOU GUYS.

169
00:14:28,865 --> 00:14:30,385
<i>Yeah, Te.</i>

170
00:14:30,465 --> 00:14:31,745
<i>So what are we supposed to do?</i>

171
00:14:31,825 --> 00:14:33,985
<i>Exactly, Neo.</i>

172
00:14:36,425 --> 00:14:38,865
-What?
-Act natural.

173
00:14:40,865 --> 00:14:42,025
Come on, help me think.

174
00:14:46,025 --> 00:14:48,465
<i>Oh, shit. We have</i>
<i>an assignment to turn in.</i>

175
00:14:48,545 --> 00:14:50,705
Yeah, that's much more natural.

176
00:14:50,785 --> 00:14:51,945
<i>Then it's settled.</i>

177
00:14:52,025 --> 00:14:54,705
<i>Tomorrow at 4:30. At the club room.</i>

178
00:14:54,785 --> 00:14:56,545
<i>Let's get it done once and for all.</i>

179
00:14:57,665 --> 00:14:58,505
LET'S GET IT DONE ONCE AND FOR ALL.

180
00:15:02,705 --> 00:15:05,745
I think… we should make them
send a sticker.

181
00:15:05,825 --> 00:15:07,225
Otherwise, they'll just say
they didn't see it.

182
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:10,745
Brilliant, my vice president.

183
00:15:11,905 --> 00:15:14,265
<i>If you've read it, send one sticker.</i>

184
00:15:14,345 --> 00:15:16,105
IF YOU'VE READ IT, SEND ONE STICKER.

185
00:15:20,225 --> 00:15:22,425
Damn it. Now it's obvious we set this up.

186
00:15:29,665 --> 00:15:31,065
One more.

187
00:15:31,145 --> 00:15:32,105
Come on, buddy.

188
00:15:32,185 --> 00:15:33,425
I've been so nervous I could barely pee.

189
00:15:35,065 --> 00:15:36,785
<i>Alright. See you then.</i>

190
00:15:38,345 --> 00:15:40,465
-So?
-Lee sounded tense as hell.

191
00:15:40,545 --> 00:15:41,905
He didn't even send a sticker.

192
00:15:41,985 --> 00:15:44,225
It's okay. At least he's coming.

193
00:15:44,305 --> 00:15:47,865
Our friendship-repair
mission won't be that hard after all.

194
00:15:50,185 --> 00:15:51,425
Awesome.

195
00:15:51,505 --> 00:15:53,345
Alright.

196
00:15:53,425 --> 00:15:55,625
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

197
00:16:28,745 --> 00:16:31,465
I think… this one's pretty serious, guys.

198
00:16:34,825 --> 00:16:36,665
I think we should talk to them separately.

199
00:16:37,345 --> 00:16:39,105
Going as a group probably won't work.

200
00:16:58,945 --> 00:17:00,785
I know about you and Ter.

201
00:17:05,585 --> 00:17:07,145
How are you holding up? Are you okay?

202
00:17:09,145 --> 00:17:10,545
I don't know.

203
00:17:13,105 --> 00:17:15,145
Forget it. You wouldn't understand.

204
00:17:15,224 --> 00:17:16,345
Come on, asshole.

205
00:17:16,985 --> 00:17:18,224
Why do you never say anything?

206
00:17:18,305 --> 00:17:20,065
Because he likes you.

207
00:17:20,145 --> 00:17:21,424
He doesn't like me.

208
00:17:22,825 --> 00:17:24,025
Don't take it out on me.

209
00:17:24,105 --> 00:17:26,265
I even let it slide when you lied to me.

210
00:17:26,345 --> 00:17:27,944
But I can't let this slide.

211
00:17:36,905 --> 00:17:38,025
Guys, calm down.

212
00:17:38,105 --> 00:17:40,585
Weren't you the one who made that rule?

213
00:17:40,665 --> 00:17:42,185
And now you're the one breaking it.

214
00:17:42,265 --> 00:17:43,705
You even lied to your friends.

215
00:17:43,785 --> 00:17:45,225
Because the rule is ridiculous.

216
00:17:45,305 --> 00:17:47,785
Who can stop themselves
from falling for someone?

217
00:17:47,865 --> 00:17:50,265
But you made that rule,
so you shouldn't be breaking it.

218
00:17:50,345 --> 00:17:51,785
Especially you, Ter.

219
00:17:51,865 --> 00:17:53,945
You're the last person who should be
saying that, you loudmouth.

220
00:17:54,025 --> 00:17:56,505
Stop it!
It's my fault for making that rule.

221
00:17:56,585 --> 00:17:57,745
That's enough.

222
00:17:57,825 --> 00:17:59,385
I'm leaving this club.

223
00:17:59,465 --> 00:18:01,425
I never wanted to be
in this damn club anyway.

224
00:18:06,545 --> 00:18:08,345
-Hey, Ter!
-Ter!

225
00:18:08,425 --> 00:18:09,705
-Putter!
-Ter!

226
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:14,745
That's enough, you assholes.

227
00:18:14,825 --> 00:18:15,945
You've gone too far.

228
00:18:16,825 --> 00:18:18,185
Just calm down.

229
00:18:18,265 --> 00:18:19,705
Aren't we friends in the end?

230
00:18:21,785 --> 00:18:24,385
Friends don't talk to each other
like this, asshole.

231
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:28,865
Then stop being my friend.
I'm the asshole.

232
00:18:34,065 --> 00:18:34,985
Lee.

233
00:18:38,105 --> 00:18:42,265
"DON'T" DATE SOMEONE CLOSE TO YOU!

234
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:11,105
It's weird without the guys around.

235
00:19:11,185 --> 00:19:12,105
Yeah, isn't it?

236
00:19:12,705 --> 00:19:14,225
Look.

237
00:19:14,305 --> 00:19:16,385
The table is so much quieter.

238
00:19:16,465 --> 00:19:18,065
Yeah.

239
00:19:18,145 --> 00:19:21,585
So… Was their fight really that bad?

240
00:19:22,265 --> 00:19:24,025
Yeah, it was pretty bad.

241
00:19:24,545 --> 00:19:26,585
So, have you talked to Ter?

242
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:29,545
He's not answering my calls,
and he won't even reply to my messages.

243
00:19:35,385 --> 00:19:37,305
What's wrong with you?

244
00:19:39,385 --> 00:19:40,585
I feel guilty.

245
00:19:41,865 --> 00:19:42,905
Guilty about what?

246
00:19:44,145 --> 00:19:48,465
At first, I was totally fangirling
when I saw Putter's post on X.

247
00:19:49,185 --> 00:19:52,465
When people dug it up, I was excited too.

248
00:19:52,985 --> 00:19:56,865
But when I saw Putter feeling so awful,
I felt even more guilty.

249
00:19:57,465 --> 00:19:59,065
Yeah, exactly.

250
00:19:59,145 --> 00:20:02,265
Maybe the universe is trying
to teach you a lesson.

251
00:20:02,345 --> 00:20:04,785
Don't let the brain rot
consume you until you fall.

252
00:20:04,865 --> 00:20:08,265
Seriously. These days, once you fall,
you don't get back up.

253
00:20:08,345 --> 00:20:09,665
Ugh.

254
00:20:10,185 --> 00:20:12,185
I already feel bad enough.

255
00:20:12,265 --> 00:20:14,625
If you feel guilty,
then go apologize to Ter.

256
00:20:14,705 --> 00:20:16,705
You can wait until the timing feels right.

257
00:20:58,465 --> 00:20:59,425
Hey.

258
00:21:00,345 --> 00:21:01,465
Yeah?

259
00:21:04,425 --> 00:21:06,225
Speak, or I'm going back to watching TV.

260
00:21:07,265 --> 00:21:08,785
Reply to your aunt's message too.

261
00:21:09,625 --> 00:21:11,185
She wants to talk to you
about architecture tutoring.

262
00:21:13,225 --> 00:21:14,585
Okay. Thanks.

263
00:21:49,065 --> 00:21:50,625
Why won't he just get some sleep?

264
00:22:58,745 --> 00:23:00,465
Shit. I'm late.

265
00:23:08,785 --> 00:23:10,585
You have P.E. first period.

266
00:23:12,945 --> 00:23:13,905
Yeah.

267
00:23:14,425 --> 00:23:16,025
I bought two lunch boxes.

268
00:23:16,585 --> 00:23:18,065
Help yourself if you get hungry.

269
00:23:18,945 --> 00:23:20,505
In case you don't have time
to grab something.

270
00:23:28,465 --> 00:23:31,345
But if you don't eat it,
put it in the fridge.

271
00:23:59,345 --> 00:24:00,705
Damn it.

272
00:24:15,065 --> 00:24:18,305
I can only refund you 50%, LeeIth,
according to the school's policy.

273
00:24:18,385 --> 00:24:20,785
That's fine. I'll explain it to my mom.

274
00:24:23,505 --> 00:24:24,465
All set.

275
00:24:26,345 --> 00:24:29,145
So, which faculty did you
decide to switch to?

276
00:24:29,825 --> 00:24:31,985
Putter said you changed your mind.

277
00:24:34,665 --> 00:24:35,585
There he is.

278
00:24:43,225 --> 00:24:45,025
LeeIth came to request a refund.

279
00:24:47,985 --> 00:24:49,865
Yeah, it's good that you came to
process the refund.

280
00:24:50,905 --> 00:24:52,945
I'll get going now. Goodbye.

281
00:25:04,665 --> 00:25:06,665
If you need to vent,
you can always talk to me, Ter.

282
00:25:07,505 --> 00:25:08,505
Okay.

283
00:25:09,265 --> 00:25:11,785
And don't forget, today's
the sketch design submission.

284
00:25:12,625 --> 00:25:13,505
Okay.

285
00:26:42,225 --> 00:26:43,905
<i>Try not to take Grab so often.</i>

286
00:26:43,985 --> 00:26:46,425
<i>It's been charging my card nonstop.</i>

287
00:26:46,505 --> 00:26:48,745
<i>I know. I saw it.</i>

288
00:27:06,265 --> 00:27:08,145
<i>Is he stalking you again?</i>

289
00:27:11,585 --> 00:27:13,145
<i>I think Lee still has feelings for you.</i>

290
00:27:13,225 --> 00:27:14,625
<i>He's just putting on an act.</i>

291
00:27:17,305 --> 00:27:19,305
<i>So what's he going to do?</i>

292
00:27:20,505 --> 00:27:21,905
<i>Calm down.</i>

293
00:27:23,585 --> 00:27:24,985
<i>You defend him too much.</i>

294
00:27:25,065 --> 00:27:26,345
<i>Think you'll get back together?</i>

295
00:27:27,905 --> 00:27:29,985
<i>We should just stay friends.</i>

296
00:27:30,065 --> 00:27:31,385
<i>It's probably for the best.</i>

297
00:27:32,585 --> 00:27:35,465
<i>I respect whatever you decide.</i>

298
00:27:35,545 --> 00:27:37,265
<i>Put that energy into practice.</i>

299
00:27:37,345 --> 00:27:38,585
<i>I'll be cheering for you.</i>

300
00:28:11,385 --> 00:28:14,545
Let the sound waves work
through your body.

301
00:28:15,265 --> 00:28:18,985
And release the emotions
you've been holding onto

302
00:28:19,585 --> 00:28:21,785
through your breath.

303
00:28:23,145 --> 00:28:25,785
Take a deep breath in.

304
00:28:29,105 --> 00:28:32,185
And breathe out slowly.

305
00:28:41,505 --> 00:28:44,505
Take a deep breath in.

306
00:28:44,585 --> 00:28:47,105
And breathe out slowly.

307
00:28:58,665 --> 00:29:00,585
Take a deep breath in.

308
00:29:07,225 --> 00:29:08,465
That's a bit too intense.

309
00:29:08,545 --> 00:29:09,905
Okay, okay.

310
00:29:17,945 --> 00:29:18,985
That's funny.

311
00:29:28,905 --> 00:29:30,065
How did that feel?

312
00:29:32,065 --> 00:29:33,265
I feel pretty good.

313
00:29:34,585 --> 00:29:35,825
I figured you'd feel better.

314
00:29:35,905 --> 00:29:37,345
You let out quite a sigh.

315
00:29:37,865 --> 00:29:39,425
You probably got it all out.

316
00:29:40,945 --> 00:29:42,265
Why are you so irritated?

317
00:29:52,105 --> 00:29:53,585
I'm happy for you.

318
00:29:54,185 --> 00:29:56,145
I'm glad you finally let it out.

319
00:29:56,225 --> 00:29:58,345
I'll go make you some cocoa.

320
00:29:58,425 --> 00:29:59,945
-Make yourself at home.
-Yes, Mom.

321
00:30:00,025 --> 00:30:00,905
Okay.

322
00:30:13,625 --> 00:30:15,265
What are we going to do about Lee?

323
00:30:15,865 --> 00:30:17,105
Read the cards for me.

324
00:30:17,905 --> 00:30:19,425
No card readings for two months.

325
00:30:19,505 --> 00:30:20,625
Why?

326
00:30:21,145 --> 00:30:23,185
You're addicted to them.

327
00:30:27,785 --> 00:30:29,865
I think I'm more addicted to you,
fortune teller.

328
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:33,225
I'm seeing you, and you want me
to go see someone else?

329
00:30:33,305 --> 00:30:34,985
Try living your own life.

330
00:30:35,065 --> 00:30:36,185
Otherwise, one day,

331
00:30:36,265 --> 00:30:38,305
you'll need to read the cards
before taking your first step.

332
00:30:38,385 --> 00:30:39,665
That'll make life difficult.

333
00:30:41,425 --> 00:30:42,545
Yeah.

334
00:30:42,625 --> 00:30:43,865
You've got a point.

335
00:30:44,625 --> 00:30:45,705
But it's hard.

336
00:30:46,305 --> 00:30:47,745
That's life.

337
00:30:47,825 --> 00:30:50,145
You never know what's going to happen.

338
00:30:50,665 --> 00:30:53,265
Even if the cards say so,
it doesn't mean it'll actually happen.

339
00:30:58,185 --> 00:30:59,385
You're pretty sharp.

340
00:30:59,945 --> 00:31:01,625
I got it all from my mom.

341
00:31:01,705 --> 00:31:02,905
I get it.

342
00:31:02,985 --> 00:31:04,185
You got your sharpness from your mom.

343
00:31:04,785 --> 00:31:06,105
You know, you're a lot like her.

344
00:31:06,185 --> 00:31:07,225
My face?

345
00:31:07,745 --> 00:31:08,985
Your vibe too.

346
00:31:09,065 --> 00:31:11,625
Like, I feel at ease around you.

347
00:31:13,545 --> 00:31:14,385
Can you say that again?

348
00:31:14,465 --> 00:31:15,345
I want to use it in the café's review.

349
00:31:15,425 --> 00:31:16,625
Sure.

350
00:31:22,465 --> 00:31:24,625
You're camera-shy for a Gen Z.

351
00:31:25,225 --> 00:31:26,145
Stop teasing me.

352
00:31:26,225 --> 00:31:29,345
Besides, no Gen Z
actually calls someone a "Gen Z."

353
00:31:29,425 --> 00:31:30,785
Only old people do.

354
00:31:40,185 --> 00:31:42,145
-So cute.
-So cute.

355
00:31:42,225 --> 00:31:43,345
Hey.

356
00:31:45,985 --> 00:31:48,905
Going on a date with the three of us…

357
00:31:48,985 --> 00:31:51,665
-You're okay with that, right?
-Sure. It's fun.

358
00:31:51,745 --> 00:31:52,905
Did you even ask me?

359
00:31:53,585 --> 00:31:55,705
-Hey, Summer.
-Wow.

360
00:31:55,785 --> 00:31:57,665
-So cute.
-It looks great on you.

361
00:31:57,745 --> 00:31:58,705
Really?

362
00:31:58,785 --> 00:32:00,265
-Is it pretty?
-Yeah.

363
00:32:01,305 --> 00:32:03,945
You two are really close.

364
00:32:04,025 --> 00:32:06,665
Well, we've known each other forever.

365
00:32:06,745 --> 00:32:08,065
Want to be close with us too?

366
00:32:09,425 --> 00:32:10,345
I'll pass.

367
00:32:11,385 --> 00:32:12,265
Don't kill the mood.

368
00:32:20,345 --> 00:32:22,265
LeeIth says that a lot, doesn't he?

369
00:32:24,545 --> 00:32:26,865
Yeah, but I don't mind.

370
00:32:30,905 --> 00:32:31,865
Hey.

371
00:32:31,945 --> 00:32:35,145
When you're with us,
you can talk about anything.

372
00:32:35,225 --> 00:32:36,585
No holding back. Don't front.

373
00:32:36,665 --> 00:32:37,505
You get me?

374
00:32:41,305 --> 00:32:42,625
I do miss him.

375
00:32:42,705 --> 00:32:44,265
Do you want to make up with him?

376
00:32:47,945 --> 00:32:50,185
Well… I don't know.

377
00:32:56,905 --> 00:32:58,785
Yeah, I do.

378
00:32:58,865 --> 00:33:00,305
If it's possible.

379
00:33:00,945 --> 00:33:02,545
That's it.

380
00:33:02,625 --> 00:33:06,545
First, you need to figure out
how you really feel.

381
00:33:06,625 --> 00:33:09,785
I can tell what you're thinking
just by looking into your eyes.

382
00:33:10,305 --> 00:33:12,225
We're so alike.

383
00:33:12,305 --> 00:33:14,425
You two are both so stubborn.

384
00:33:15,185 --> 00:33:16,705
That hit hard.

385
00:33:17,345 --> 00:33:18,625
You're so good at dealing with

386
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:20,065
people's problems, but not your own.

387
00:33:20,145 --> 00:33:21,665
That's not true.

388
00:33:21,745 --> 00:33:23,625
Whenever I want you to make up with me,

389
00:33:23,705 --> 00:33:25,105
I've already planned everything.

390
00:33:26,305 --> 00:33:28,625
You never realized
I got you wrapped around my finger.

391
00:33:29,545 --> 00:33:31,665
Hey, did you two forget about me?

392
00:33:31,745 --> 00:33:33,585
See? You forgot your friend.

393
00:33:33,665 --> 00:33:36,425
-Whoops, sorry.
-Sorry.

394
00:33:36,505 --> 00:33:37,545
I'm kidding.

395
00:33:37,625 --> 00:33:39,545
But seriously, thanks, you guys.

396
00:33:39,625 --> 00:33:41,425
I feel a lot better now
that I've talked about it.

397
00:33:41,505 --> 00:33:43,585
If you get the chance, give it a shot.

398
00:33:43,665 --> 00:33:44,905
Or you'll regret it.

399
00:33:48,065 --> 00:33:49,305
Did you tell him that story yet?

400
00:33:49,385 --> 00:33:51,265
About when you confessed
your feelings to me.

401
00:33:51,345 --> 00:33:52,585
Yeah, I did.

402
00:33:52,665 --> 00:33:53,985
How much did you tell him?

403
00:33:54,065 --> 00:33:55,785
Everything.

404
00:33:55,865 --> 00:33:58,505
Did you tell him you cried too?

405
00:33:58,585 --> 00:33:59,465
No.

406
00:34:00,065 --> 00:34:02,825
Back then, Proud cried so hard,

407
00:34:02,905 --> 00:34:05,545
she was bright red
and all her coolness was gone.

408
00:34:05,625 --> 00:34:07,025
Stop gossiping about me already.

409
00:34:07,105 --> 00:34:09,065
My bad. Sorry.

410
00:34:11,865 --> 00:34:13,824
Hey, hey, hey! That's so cute.

411
00:34:27,225 --> 00:34:29,705
4 DAYS BEFORE THE COMPETITION

412
00:34:33,545 --> 00:34:36,585
Lee. Are you going
to watch Putter compete?

413
00:34:38,625 --> 00:34:40,945
I'm busy. Cheer him on for me.

414
00:34:42,145 --> 00:34:43,304
Lee!

415
00:34:44,465 --> 00:34:45,625
Come on, just go.

416
00:34:46,145 --> 00:34:48,465
-Will you?
-I'm busy.

417
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:54,545
Damn it.

418
00:34:55,145 --> 00:34:56,185
Hey, Bro.

419
00:34:57,305 --> 00:34:58,345
Bro.

420
00:34:58,425 --> 00:34:59,905
Are you going to watch Putter compete?

421
00:35:00,625 --> 00:35:01,465
Let me think about it.

422
00:35:01,545 --> 00:35:02,785
Hey, wait.

423
00:35:03,905 --> 00:35:05,345
Jia's going too.

424
00:35:06,185 --> 00:35:07,345
So?

425
00:35:07,425 --> 00:35:09,105
Well, you two have gotten
pretty close lately,

426
00:35:09,185 --> 00:35:10,545
so I invited him too.

427
00:35:13,025 --> 00:35:16,225
You want me to go because you
want me to make up with Putter, right?

428
00:35:17,585 --> 00:35:18,705
Okay.

429
00:35:18,785 --> 00:35:21,025
I'll be straight with you. Yeah.

430
00:35:21,665 --> 00:35:23,545
But won't that just make things worse?

431
00:35:24,145 --> 00:35:25,625
If he still likes me.

432
00:35:26,225 --> 00:35:27,665
You're pretty confident, huh?

433
00:35:28,185 --> 00:35:29,465
I'm just thinking ahead.

434
00:35:29,545 --> 00:35:32,905
Besides, if Lee sees me,
he'll take it out on me again. Damn it.

435
00:35:32,985 --> 00:35:34,905
Lee isn't going.

436
00:35:37,265 --> 00:35:38,545
Yeah, I'll think about it.

437
00:35:44,065 --> 00:35:44,945
Seriously…

438
00:35:45,025 --> 00:35:46,425
You couldn't do it?

439
00:35:46,505 --> 00:35:48,265
I've got nothing left to say.

440
00:35:49,465 --> 00:35:55,105
Well, Proud and Summer said
Putter's still worried about you guys.

441
00:35:55,185 --> 00:35:59,065
If… you two…
could work things out, that'd be nice.

442
00:35:59,145 --> 00:36:01,585
Since when was that my responsibility?

443
00:36:02,705 --> 00:36:05,185
They said if the club has fewer
than six members,

444
00:36:05,265 --> 00:36:06,545
it's definitely getting shut down.

445
00:36:07,785 --> 00:36:09,065
Say bye-bye to the room.

446
00:36:13,465 --> 00:36:14,945
-Good luck.
-Good luck.

447
00:36:19,825 --> 00:36:22,545
If not for our friendship,
then I'll do it for the club.

448
00:36:29,585 --> 00:36:30,745
<i>Prepare Plan B.</i>

449
00:36:31,985 --> 00:36:34,745
<i>If we can't do it the easy way,</i>
<i>we'll have to use another tactic.</i>

450
00:36:36,745 --> 00:36:37,945
<i>Tactic?</i>

451
00:36:59,945 --> 00:37:01,545
-What the hell is this?
-Grab him.

452
00:37:01,625 --> 00:37:03,265
-Let me go!
-Stay still.

453
00:37:03,345 --> 00:37:05,985
-Get over here.
-Hey, hey, hey!

454
00:37:06,065 --> 00:37:08,905
-Stop struggling! Stop struggling!
-Damn it, I'm heavy!

455
00:37:08,985 --> 00:37:10,185
Turn him around! Turn him around!

456
00:37:10,265 --> 00:37:12,585
-Go, go!
-Past the chair! Past the chair!

457
00:37:12,665 --> 00:37:13,825
-Yeah, that's it!
-What the hell is this?

458
00:37:13,905 --> 00:37:15,785
-Hold him down! Hold him down!
-Grab him! Grab him!

459
00:37:15,865 --> 00:37:17,185
-Stop struggling!
-Let me go!

460
00:37:17,265 --> 00:37:18,465
This is your Plan B? Your "tactic"?

461
00:37:18,545 --> 00:37:20,465
Yeah. By "tactic," I mean brute force.

462
00:37:21,225 --> 00:37:22,625
-Damn it!
-Stay still!

463
00:37:23,465 --> 00:37:25,345
We've already talked
things through with Indy.

464
00:37:25,425 --> 00:37:26,385
You're the only one left.

465
00:37:26,465 --> 00:37:27,985
Yeah, and you're about to compete.

466
00:37:28,065 --> 00:37:29,265
So you won't have any regrets.

467
00:37:29,345 --> 00:37:30,305
Just get it over with, okay?

468
00:37:30,385 --> 00:37:32,665
-Do you get it?
-Do you get it?

469
00:37:33,705 --> 00:37:34,785
-Go.
-Go, go, go!

470
00:37:35,385 --> 00:37:37,305
-Damn it! I can't get my shirt off!
-Hurry up!

471
00:37:37,385 --> 00:37:38,585
Come on! Come on!

472
00:37:39,105 --> 00:37:40,505
You bunch of kidnappers.

473
00:37:44,665 --> 00:37:46,265
Don't you think they're overdoing it?

474
00:37:47,305 --> 00:37:48,545
Big time.

475
00:37:56,185 --> 00:37:57,545
Here, let me fix it for you.

476
00:38:24,465 --> 00:38:25,665
Thanks.

477
00:38:36,025 --> 00:38:37,505
I'm sorry too, Putter.

478
00:38:38,385 --> 00:38:41,385
That day, I… didn't mean it.

479
00:38:43,825 --> 00:38:45,545
I wasn't that mad at you anyway.

480
00:38:51,865 --> 00:38:52,985
And…

481
00:38:55,105 --> 00:38:56,425
what about your other feelings?

482
00:39:00,465 --> 00:39:01,505
Well…

483
00:39:02,025 --> 00:39:03,465
I did have feelings for you.

484
00:39:12,225 --> 00:39:13,505
Crap, sorry. Are you okay?

485
00:39:13,585 --> 00:39:16,145
I'm fine. It's all good. See you around.

486
00:39:18,665 --> 00:39:22,145
<i>Back then, I fell for your kindness.</i>

487
00:39:24,465 --> 00:39:25,465
<i>Lee…</i>

488
00:39:33,345 --> 00:39:34,625
<i>My heart was really racing.</i>

489
00:39:35,145 --> 00:39:36,665
<i>I thought you were going</i>
<i>to ask for my Instagram.</i>

490
00:39:46,145 --> 00:39:49,265
Even though I knew you already liked Faye,

491
00:39:50,025 --> 00:39:52,065
my feelings had already taken over.

492
00:39:59,425 --> 00:40:01,865
So… what about now?

493
00:40:11,225 --> 00:40:13,025
I… don't have feelings for you anymore.

494
00:40:13,585 --> 00:40:14,705
So you can relax.

495
00:40:15,545 --> 00:40:17,305
I see you as 100% a friend.

496
00:40:24,625 --> 00:40:25,945
It's just…

497
00:40:26,745 --> 00:40:28,225
I'm okay now, but…

498
00:40:28,745 --> 00:40:30,305
I was afraid you'd feel uncomfortable.

499
00:40:31,545 --> 00:40:32,585
Because…

500
00:40:33,345 --> 00:40:36,225
I understand what it's like to have
feelings for someone,

501
00:40:37,185 --> 00:40:38,545
and it feels like you're given hope.

502
00:40:39,905 --> 00:40:41,065
Damn… you know how that feels?

503
00:40:42,945 --> 00:40:44,065
Shit.

504
00:40:44,905 --> 00:40:46,265
Talking about this really gets to me.

505
00:40:47,945 --> 00:40:50,385
So, there's nothing
between us anymore, right?

506
00:40:50,905 --> 00:40:52,225
We've cleared things up.

507
00:40:53,345 --> 00:40:54,825
Now it's just your friend.

508
00:40:58,345 --> 00:40:59,705
Just give him some time.

509
00:41:00,225 --> 00:41:03,385
That idiot…
he takes everything way too far.

510
00:41:03,465 --> 00:41:05,145
He'll calm down eventually.

511
00:41:10,745 --> 00:41:11,905
Thanks.

512
00:41:16,225 --> 00:41:19,505
I'm sorry for being so immature.

513
00:41:23,265 --> 00:41:24,385
Come on.

514
00:41:26,065 --> 00:41:27,985
Uh… you guys are done talking, right?

515
00:41:28,065 --> 00:41:29,625
No one's kissing or anything, right?

516
00:41:29,705 --> 00:41:31,265
We were just about to come in.

517
00:41:31,865 --> 00:41:33,305
Yeah, we're good.

518
00:41:33,385 --> 00:41:34,305
Come on in.

519
00:41:38,425 --> 00:41:39,865
-You guys are the best!
-The best!

520
00:41:39,945 --> 00:41:41,665
You guys are the best!

521
00:41:41,745 --> 00:41:44,065
You idiot! I told you we're friends.

522
00:41:46,465 --> 00:41:47,665
Okay, okay.

523
00:41:48,665 --> 00:41:50,425
Now you can focus on your tournament
with peace of mind, buddy.

524
